    "description": "The 62 AW Safety office provides consultation, investigation, and inspection support to the Air Force contingent on Joint Base Lewis-McChord. ",
    "references": "29 CFR 1904\n29 CFR Part 1910 - Occupational Safety and Health Standards (General Industry Standards)\n29 CFR Part 1926 - Safety and Health Regulations for Construction\nDODI 6055.04\nDODI 6055.07\nDAFI 91-202 - The Department of the Air Force (DAF) Mishap Prevention Program\nDAFI 91-203\nDAFI 91-204\nDiscipline specific 91- series manuals\n",
    "jhaNotes": "Personnel assigned to the 62 AW Safety office will conduct their duties throughout the Wing. They may be exposed or working in the vicinity of the following operations: construction, material handling, chemical usage, aircraft maintenance, vehicle maintenance, airfield systems repair, explosive operations, and more. Safety personnel shall always be aware of their surroundings when performing inspections, and avoid putting themselves in hazardous situations. ",
    "emergencyNumbers": "Police, Fire, and Medical Emergencies: 911\n446 Wing Safety- COM: (253) 982-5307 / DSN: 382-5307\nMaintenance Operations Control- COM: (253) 982-3336 / DSN: 382-3336\nCommand Post- COM: (253) 982-2635 / DSN: 382-2635\nSecurity Forces LE Desk-  COM: (253) 982-5624",
